From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jess <15219610+jesscarter@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:08:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mproton: win32u: Let WINE_EMULATE_MODESET override the
 EmulateModeset setting.

The display mode list is built by whichever process refreshes the display
cache, usually explorer.exe, so an AppDefaults\<game>.exe\X11 Driver key
does not reach it; only the prefix-wide key does. An environment variable is
seen by every process of a launch and leaves the prefix untouched, so a
launcher can turn emulated modesetting on for one game.

With it on, the mode list is win32u's virtual one, which has the usual 16:9,
4:3 and 16:10 sizes up to the host mode. macOS lists only the panel's own
scaled modes (on a 1470x956 MacBook Air none is 16:9), and games that only
offer 16:9 resolutions (Castlevania: Belmont's Curse) show an empty list.
---
 dlls/win32u/sysparams.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
index 1fdb691a112..9476acd164d 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -6047,6 +6047,7 @@ void sysparams_init(void)
     pthread_mutexattr_t attr;
     HKEY hkey, appkey = 0;
     DWORD len;
+    const char *env;
 
     static const WCHAR oneW[] = {'1',0};
     static const WCHAR x11driverW[] = {'\\','X','1','1',' ','D','r','i','v','e','r',0};
@@ -6147,6 +6148,11 @@ void sysparams_init(void)
         decorated_mode = IS_OPTION_TRUE( buffer[0] );
     if (!get_config_key( hkey, appkey, "EmulateModeset", buffer, sizeof(buffer) ))
         emulate_modeset = IS_OPTION_TRUE( buffer[0] );
+    /* The display mode list is built by whichever process refreshes the display cache
+     * (usually explorer.exe), so a per-application key does not reach it. An environment
+     * variable is seen by every process of a launch and leaves the prefix untouched. */
+    if ((env = getenv( "WINE_EMULATE_MODESET" )) && *env)
+        emulate_modeset = IS_OPTION_TRUE( env[0] );
 
 #undef IS_OPTION_TRUE
 
